  "live_records": {
    "q-134161": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134161",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{4,\\,4,\\,-4,\\,4\\},\\,y=\\{-1,\\,-2,\\,7,\\,4\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+4+(-4)+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-1)+(-2)+7+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-2)(-1-2)+(4-2)(-2-2)+(-4-2)(7-2)+(4-2)(4-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2)(-3)+(2)(-4)+(-6)(5)+(2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[-6-8-30+4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-40) \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
