    "q-134173": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134173",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "| **Time Spent Practicing, \nin hours ($x$)** | $4$ | $5$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Points Scored ($y$)** | $4$ | $8$ | $12$ | $16$ |\n\nThe table above shows Mary's time practicing her jump shot each week and the number of points she scores in the Friday varsity basketball game. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=10.$",
      "worked_solution": "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-6)(4-10)+(5-6)(8-10)+(7-6)(12-10)+(8-6)(16-10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-6)+(-1)(-2)+(1)(2)+(2)(6)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+2+2+12] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
